cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SAKE-DT, please cite this software release."
type: software
title: "SAKE-DT: Spectral Autodiff Kernel Expansion for Duhamel Transport"
version: "v0.2-sake-autodiff-dimer"
date-released: "2026-08-19"
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: Bittner
    given-names: Eric R.
repository-code: "https://github.com/ebitnet65/Duhamel_Transport"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/ebitnet65/Duhamel_Transport/releases/tag/v0.2-sake-autodiff-dimer"
abstract: >
  SAKE-DT is a Spectral Autodiff Kernel Expansion framework for Duhamel
  transport of Liouville-space nonlinear-response pathways. This release
  provides model-agnostic transport and Duhamel-expansion machinery, a
  JAX/autodiff Liouvillian derivative backend, and a four-level su(2) x su(2)
  exciton-dimer validation workflow through third order.
keywords:
  - Duhamel expansion
  - Liouville space
  - autodiff
  - JAX
  - nonlinear spectroscopy
  - two-dimensional spectroscopy
  - exciton dimer
  - pathway transport
  - response functions
